I've had one death due to liches, but I can't understand how they could
be a serious threat to a good character.

My strategy is:

- Ring-of-conflict them against another monster (preferably a cold
resistant one), then walk up and kill them.

- Throw things at them.  Cockatrice corpses are good for this.  Or zap
wands.

- Like, run away!  By the time you meet any liches, you are fast and
invisible, right?  And telepathic, so a lich never takes you by
surprise.

- They are not really very tough to fight, they just have that "destroy
armor" spell.  So take off your shield of reflection or gauntlets of
dexterity before fighting them.

